-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part wra1 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- wra1-seat.l4: Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), Part 1, Schedules 1, 2, 5 and 6 -- THE SEAT LAYER, part wra1.
-- LAYER 2: it asks the questions of the person and calls the layer-1 rules; no rule is restated here.
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script, not the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who claims, receives or is moved to universal credit, or whose benefits are capped (a person who claims
-- personal independence payment or is capped is served by the other parts: wra3 and wra4).
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes yes/no, numbers, dates and the modules' own choices, one for each fact the person can
-- state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. The records the layer-1 rules expect (a person, two people,
-- a period) are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers; a record field that the rule called never
-- reads is given a fixed placeholder, with a comment saying so.
-- A fact the person cannot state because only regulations make it (a prescribed amount, a prescribed description) is either
-- asked as "yes / no / I do not know" (the type `s 1(1) what I know`) or passed on as NOTHING with a comment. Where the answer
-- depends on such a value and the person does not know it, the answer is NOTHING: the Act does not say.
--
-- Reading an answer (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed and not ruled by a lawyer): JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is no, in the text's
-- own words or from a regulation the person says exists; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer this on the facts given".
--
-- Schedule 2 has no printed paragraph numbers, so its questions begin "Under schedule 2 (" and name the host Act's provision.

§ `Helpers shared by the questions`

-- "Yes / no / I do not know" for a fact only regulations decide. The label is the first provision of the Act; the type is used by many questions.
DECLARE `s 1(1) what I know` IS ONE OF
    `s 1(1) what I know: yes`
    `s 1(1) what I know: no`
    `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know`

GIVEN know IS A `s 1(1) what I know`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` MEANS
    CONSIDER know
    WHEN `s 1(1) what I know: yes` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1(1) what I know: no` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` THEN NOTHING

-- A person whose age and place a rule reads.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, place IS A Place
GIVETH A Person
`s 1(1) seat helper: me` MEANS Person WITH
    `reference` IS "me"
    `age in years` IS age
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 2000     -- placeholder: no rule called from this layer reads it
    `where the person is` IS place
    `where the person lives` IS place

-- A person whose age and place no rule called with it reads (s 39 reads only the three facts of the relationship).
GIVEN reference IS A STRING
GIVETH A Person
`s 1(1) seat helper: a person no rule reads` MEANS Person WITH
    `reference` IS reference
    `age in years` IS 30                -- placeholder: s 1(2) and s 39 do not read it
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 2000     -- placeholder: no rule called from this layer reads it
    `where the person is` IS Wales       -- placeholder: s 1(2) and s 39 do not read it
    `where the person lives` IS Wales    -- placeholder: s 1(2) and s 39 do not read it

GIVEN married IS A BOOLEAN, household IS A BOOLEAN, living IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Two people`
`s 1(1) seat helper: the two of us` MEANS `Two people` WITH
    `the first person` IS `s 1(1) seat helper: a person no rule reads` "me"
    `the second person` IS `s 1(1) seat helper: a person no rule reads` "my partner"
    `their relationship` IS `Relationship of two people` WITH
        `married to each other or civil partners of each other` IS married
        `members of the same household` IS household
        `living together as if married or civil partners` IS living

-- The five basic conditions of s 4(1), asked of the person; the regulation-made values are passed on as NOTHING.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
      `reached the qualifying age` IS A BOOLEAN
      place IS A Place
      education IS A `s 1(1) what I know`
      `accepted the most up-to-date version` IS A BOOLEAN
      `accepted it in the manner prescribed` IS A `s 1(1) what I know`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) seat helper: I meet the basic conditions` MEANS
    `s 4(1) the person meets the basic conditions`
        (`s 4(1)(a) the person is at least 18 years old` (`s 1(1) seat helper: me` age place) NOTHING)
        (JUST (`s 4(1)(b) the person has not reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` `reached the qualifying age`))
        (JUST (`s 4(1)(c) the person is in Great Britain` (`s 1(1) seat helper: me` age place) NOTHING NOTHING))
        (`s 4(1)(d) the person is not receiving education` (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` education) NOTHING)
        (`s 4(1)(e) the person has accepted a claimant commitment`
            (`s 14(5) the claimant accepts the claimant commitment` `accepted the most up-to-date version` (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `accepted it in the manner prescribed`))
            NOTHING)
        NOTHING
    -- NOTHING passed on: the age regulations prescribe under s 4(3), the regulations that treat a person as in or out of Great
    -- Britain or education or as having accepted the commitment (s 4(5)-(7)), a temporary absence they disregard, and the
    -- exceptions of s 4(2): none of them is among the sources.

§ `Part 1 Chapter 1 -- Universal credit: entitlement`

-- s 1(2)
@export May universal credit be awarded to me, alone or with my partner?
GIVEN `I am claiming jointly with my partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming universal credit jointly with your partner? (No if you are claiming alone.)
      `I am a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are claiming alone: are you a member of a couple, that is, married to or a civil partner of someone, or living with someone as if married or civil partners, in the same household? (Say no if you are claiming jointly.)
      `we are married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are claiming jointly: are the two of you married to each other or civil partners of each other?
      `we are members of the same household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are claiming jointly: are the two of you members of the same household?
      `we are living together as if married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are claiming jointly: are you living together as if you were married or civil partners?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1(2), may universal credit be awarded to me` IS
    `s 1(2) universal credit may be awarded to these claimants` `the claimants` `I am a member of a couple`
    WHERE
        `the claimants` MEANS
            IF `I am claiming jointly with my partner`
            THEN `joint claimants` (`s 1(1) seat helper: the two of us` `we are married or civil partners` `we are members of the same household` `we are living together as if married or civil partners`)
            ELSE `a single claimant` (`s 1(1) seat helper: a person no rule reads` "me")

-- s 4(1)(a)
@export Am I old enough to meet the age condition for universal credit?
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in completed years?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 4(1)(a), am I at least 18 years old` IS
    -- NOTHING passed on: the different minimum age regulations may prescribe for a case (s 4(3)) is not among the sources
    `s 4(1)(a) the person is at least 18 years old` (`s 1(1) seat helper: me` `my age in years` `England outside Greater London`) NOTHING     -- placeholder place: s 4(1)(a) does not read it

-- s 4(1)(b)
@export Have I reached the qualifying age for state pension credit?
GIVEN `I have reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached the age at which you can claim state pension credit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 4(1)(b), have I not yet reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS
    `s 4(1)(b) the person has not reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` `I have reached the qualifying age for state pension credit`

-- s 4(1)(c)
@export Am I in Great Britain?
GIVEN `where I am` IS A Place @desc Where are you now?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 4(1)(c), am I in Great Britain` IS
    `s 4(1)(c) the place is in Great Britain` `where I am`

-- s 4(1)
@export Do I meet the basic conditions for universal credit?
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in completed years?
      `I have reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached the age at which you can claim state pension credit?
      `where I am` IS A Place @desc Where are you now?
      `I am receiving education` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Are you receiving education, as the regulations define that?
      `I have accepted the most up-to-date version of my claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you accepted the most up-to-date version of your claimant commitment?
      `I accepted it in the manner prescribed` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Did you accept it in the manner the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 4(1), do I meet the basic conditions` IS
    `s 4(1) seat helper: I meet the basic conditions`
        `my age in years` `I have reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` `where I am`
        `I am receiving education` `I have accepted the most up-to-date version of my claimant commitment` `I accepted it in the manner prescribed`

-- s 3(1)
@export Am I entitled to universal credit as a single claimant?
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in completed years?
      `I have reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached the age at which you can claim state pension credit?
      `where I am` IS A Place @desc Where are you now?
      `I am receiving education` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Are you receiving education, as the regulations define that?
      `I have accepted the most up-to-date version of my claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you accepted the most up-to-date version of your claimant commitment?
      `I accepted it in the manner prescribed` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Did you accept it in the manner the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 3(1), am I entitled to universal credit` IS
    `s 3(1) the single claimant is entitled to universal credit`
        (`s 4(1) seat helper: I meet the basic conditions`
            `my age in years` `I have reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` `where I am`
            `I am receiving education` `I have accepted the most up-to-date version of my claimant commitment` `I accepted it in the manner prescribed`)
        (`s 5(1) the financial conditions for a single claimant are met`
            (`s 5(1)(a) the claimant's capital is not greater than the prescribed amount` 0 NOTHING)     -- the capital figure is not read while the prescribed amount is NOTHING
            (`s 5(1)(b) the amount payable would not be less than the prescribed minimum` NOTHING NOTHING))
    -- NOTHING passed on: the prescribed amount of capital (s 5(1)(a)) and the prescribed minimum (s 5(1)(b)) are for regulations

-- s 8(1)
@export What is the amount of my award of universal credit for an assessment period?
GIVEN `the maximum amount, the total of my elements` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum amount of your award for the assessment period (the total of the elements in your award)?
      `the amount deducted for my earned income` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is deducted from your award for your earned income?
      `the amount deducted for my unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is deducted from your award for your unearned income?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 8(1), what is the amount of my award for the period` IS
    `s 8(1) the amount of the award of universal credit for the period` (JUST `the maximum amount, the total of my elements`) (JUST `the amount deducted for my earned income`) (JUST `the amount deducted for my unearned income`)

§ `Part 1 Chapter 2 -- Claimant responsibilities`

-- s 14(5)
@export Have I accepted my claimant commitment?
GIVEN `I have accepted the most up-to-date version` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you accepted the most up-to-date version of your claimant commitment?
      `I accepted it in the manner prescribed` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Did you accept it in the manner the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 14(5), have I accepted my claimant commitment` IS
    `s 14(5) the claimant accepts the claimant commitment` `I have accepted the most up-to-date version` (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `I accepted it in the manner prescribed`)

-- s 19(6)
@export Am I the responsible carer for my child?
GIVEN `I am a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a couple? (No if you are a single person.)
      `I am responsible for the child` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Are you responsible for the child, as the regulations define that?
      `my partner is responsible for the child` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Is your partner responsible for the child, as the regulations define that? (Leave as "I do not know" if you are a single person.)
      `my partner and I have jointly nominated me as responsible for the child` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Have you and your partner jointly nominated you as the person responsible for the child, as the regulations provide?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 19(6), am I the responsible carer for my child` IS
    `s 19(6) the person is the responsible carer for the child` `I am a member of a couple`
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `I am responsible for the child`)
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `my partner is responsible for the child`)
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `my partner and I have jointly nominated me as responsible for the child`)

-- s 13(3), with ss 19(2), 20(1), 21(1)
@export Which group of claimants am I in, for work-related requirements?
GIVEN `I have limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have limited capability for work and work-related activity?
      `I have regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person?
      `I am the responsible carer for a child under 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the responsible carer for a child under the age of 1?
      `I am the responsible carer for a child aged 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the responsible carer for a child who is aged 1?
      `I am the responsible carer for a child aged 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the responsible carer for a child who is aged 2?
      `I have limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have limited capability for work?
      `regulations place me in section 19` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do the regulations describe you as a claimant who is subject to no work-related requirements (section 19(2)(d))?
      `regulations place me in section 20` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do the regulations describe you as a claimant who is subject to a work-focused interview requirement only (section 20(1)(b))?
      `regulations place me in section 21` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do the regulations describe you as a claimant who is subject to a work preparation requirement (section 21(1)(b))?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Group of claimants by requirement`
DECIDE `Under section 13(3), which group of claimants am I in` IS
    `s 13(3) the group the claimant falls into` `section 19` `section 20` `section 21`
    WHERE
        `section 19` MEANS
            `s 19(2) the claimant falls within section 19`
                (JUST `I have limited capability for work and work-related activity`)
                (JUST `I have regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person`)
                (JUST `I am the responsible carer for a child under 1`)
                (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `regulations place me in section 19`)
        `section 20` MEANS
            `s 20(1) the claimant falls within section 20`
                (JUST `I am the responsible carer for a child aged 1`)
                (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `regulations place me in section 20`)
        `section 21` MEANS
            `s 21(1) the claimant falls within section 21` `section 19` `section 20`
                (JUST `I have limited capability for work`)
                (JUST `I am the responsible carer for a child aged 2`)
                (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `regulations place me in section 21`)

-- s 19(1)
@export If I am in the group with no work-related requirements, may the Secretary of State impose one on me?
GIVEN `I fall within section 19` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do you fall within section 19, that is, are you a claimant who has limited capability for work and work-related activity, has regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person, is the responsible carer for a child under 1, or is of a prescribed description?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 19(1), may the Secretary of State impose a work-related requirement on me` IS
    `s 19(1) the Secretary of State may impose a work-related requirement on the claimant` (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `I fall within section 19`)

-- s 20(2)
@export If I am in the group with a work-focused interview requirement only, may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me?
GIVEN `I fall within section 20` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do you fall within section 20, that is, are you the responsible carer for a child who is aged 1, or of a prescribed description?
      `the requirement` IS A `Work-related requirement` @desc Which work-related requirement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 20(2), may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` IS
    `s 20(2) the Secretary of State may impose this requirement on the claimant` (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `I fall within section 20`) `the requirement`

-- s 21(2)
@export If I am in the group with a work preparation requirement, may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me?
GIVEN `I fall within section 21` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do you fall within section 21, that is, not within section 19 or 20 and either limited in capability for work, the responsible carer for a child aged 2, or of a prescribed description?
      `the requirement` IS A `Work-related requirement` @desc Which work-related requirement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 21(2), may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` IS
    `s 21(2) the Secretary of State may impose this requirement on the claimant` (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `I fall within section 21`) `the requirement`

-- s 22(2)
@export If I am in the group with all work-related requirements, must the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me?
GIVEN `I fall within section 22` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do you fall within section 22, that is, not within section 19, 20 or 21?
      `prescribed circumstances apply to me` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do the circumstances that regulations prescribe as an exception apply to you?
      `the requirement` IS A `Work-related requirement` @desc Which work-related requirement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 22(2), must the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` IS
    `s 22(2) the Secretary of State must impose this requirement on the claimant`
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `I fall within section 22`)
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `prescribed circumstances apply to me`)
        `the requirement`

-- s 22(3)
@export If I am in the group with all work-related requirements, may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me?
GIVEN `I fall within section 22` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do you fall within section 22, that is, not within section 19, 20 or 21?
      `the requirement` IS A `Work-related requirement` @desc Which work-related requirement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 22(3), may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` IS
    `s 22(3) the Secretary of State may impose this requirement on the claimant` (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `I fall within section 22`) `the requirement`

-- s 24(4)
@export Will I be told of a requirement in the way the Secretary of State decides?
GIVEN `my claimant commitment includes the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement included in your claimant commitment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 24(4), is notice of the requirement in the manner the Secretary of State may determine` IS
    `s 24(4) notification is in the manner the Secretary of State may determine` `my claimant commitment includes the requirement`

-- s 24(5)
@export Can another requirement be imposed on me during the 13 weeks after a victim of domestic violence's requirement ceased?
GIVEN `the first day of the 13 weeks` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the 13 weeks begin?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `prescribed circumstances apply to me` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do the circumstances that regulations prescribe for this protection apply to you?
      `I have recently been a victim of domestic violence` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Have you recently been a victim of domestic violence, as the regulations define that?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 24(5)(b), may the Secretary of State impose another requirement on me on that day` IS
    `s 24(5)(b) the Secretary of State may impose another requirement on the day`
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `prescribed circumstances apply to me`)
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `I have recently been a victim of domestic violence`)
        (`s 24(5) the period of 13 weeks` `the first day of the 13 weeks`)
        `the day I am asking about`

-- s 26(2)
@export Is my failure a higher-level sanctionable failure?
GIVEN `what I failed to do` IS A `s 26(2) kind of failure` @desc What did you fail to do?
      `I fall within section 22` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do you fall within section 22, that is, not within section 19, 20 or 21?
      `I had a good reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a good reason?
      `the placement was of a description regulations prescribe` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc If you failed to undertake a work placement: was it of a description the regulations prescribe?
      `I ceased work or lost pay by reason of misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you ceased paid work or lost pay: was it by reason of misconduct?
      `I ceased work or lost pay voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you ceased paid work or lost pay: was it voluntarily?
      `the loss of pay is disregarded` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc If you lost pay: is the loss below the level the regulations set for disregarding it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 26` IS
    `s 26(2) the failure is sanctionable under section 26` `what I failed to do`
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `I fall within section 22`)
        `I had a good reason`
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `the placement was of a description regulations prescribe`)
        `I ceased work or lost pay by reason of misconduct`
        `I ceased work or lost pay voluntarily`
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `the loss of pay is disregarded`)

-- s 26(6)(b)
@export Does the reduction of my award last no more than three years?
GIVEN `the first day of the reduction` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the reduction begin?
      `the last day of the reduction` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the reduction end?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26(6)(b), does the period of my reduction not exceed three years` IS
    `s 26(6)(b) the period of the reduction does not exceed three years`
        (Period WITH `first day` IS `the first day of the reduction`, `last day` IS `the last day of the reduction`)

-- s 27(2)
@export Is my failure a sanctionable failure under the other sanctions?
GIVEN `I failed to comply with a work-related requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with a work-related requirement?
      `I failed to comply with a requirement under section 23` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with a requirement to attend an interview, provide information or report a change (section 23)?
      `I had a good reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a good reason?
      `the failure is also sanctionable under section 26` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Is the same failure also a higher-level sanctionable failure under section 26?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 27(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 27` IS
    `s 27(2) the failure is sanctionable under section 27`
        `I failed to comply with a work-related requirement` `I failed to comply with a requirement under section 23` `I had a good reason`
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `the failure is also sanctionable under section 26`)

-- s 27(5)(b)
@export Can a fixed-period reduction last this many days?
GIVEN `the length of the fixed period in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days does the fixed period last?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 27(5)(b), does the fixed period not exceed 26 weeks` IS
    `s 27(5)(b) the fixed period does not exceed 26 weeks` `the length of the fixed period in days`

-- s 28(1)
@export May I be paid a hardship payment?
GIVEN `regulations provide for hardship payments` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do the regulations provide for hardship payments?
      `my award is reduced under section 26 or 27` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your award reduced under section 26 or 27?
      `I am or will be in hardship` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Are you, or will you be, in hardship, as the regulations define that?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 28(1), may a hardship payment be made to me` IS
    `s 28(1) a hardship payment may be made to the claimant`
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `regulations provide for hardship payments`)
        `my award is reduced under section 26 or 27`
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `I am or will be in hardship`)

-- s 29(1)
@export May this person exercise the Secretary of State's functions about my requirements?
GIVEN `who is acting` IS A Authority @desc Who is acting?
      `the Secretary of State has authorised them for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State authorised them to exercise these functions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 29(1), may this person exercise the functions of the Secretary of State under sections 13 to 25` IS
    `s 29(1) this authority may exercise the Secretary of State's functions under sections 13 to 25` `who is acting` `the Secretary of State has authorised them for the purpose`

§ `Part 1 Chapter 3 -- Supplementary and general`

-- s 33(1)
@export Has my old benefit been abolished?
GIVEN `my old benefit` IS A Benefit @desc Which benefit did you receive before?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 33(1), has my old benefit been abolished` IS
    `s 33(1) the benefit is abolished` `my old benefit`

-- s 37(1)
@export Do I have limited capability for work?
GIVEN `my capability for work is limited by my physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your capability for work limited by your physical or mental condition?
      `it is not reasonable to require me to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Because of that limit, is it not reasonable to require you to work?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 37(1), do I have limited capability for work on the Act's own test` IS
    `s 37(1) the claimant has limited capability for work on the Act's own test` `my capability for work is limited by my physical or mental condition` `it is not reasonable to require me to work`

-- s 37(2)
@export Do I have limited capability for work-related activity?
GIVEN `my capability for work-related activity is limited by my physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your capability for work-related activity limited by your physical or mental condition?
      `it is not reasonable to require me to undertake work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Because of that limit, is it not reasonable to require you to undertake work-related activity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 37(2), do I have limited capability for work-related activity on the Act's own test` IS
    `s 37(2) the claimant has limited capability for work-related activity on the Act's own test` `my capability for work-related activity is limited by my physical or mental condition` `it is not reasonable to require me to undertake work-related activity`

-- s 39(1)
@export Are my partner and I a couple?
GIVEN `we are married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and the other person married to each other or civil partners of each other?
      `we are members of the same household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and the other person members of the same household?
      `we are living together as if married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and the other person living together as if you were married or civil partners?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 39(1), are the other person and I a couple` IS
    `s 39(1) the two people are a couple` (`s 1(1) seat helper: the two of us` `we are married or civil partners` `we are members of the same household` `we are living together as if married or civil partners`)

-- s 39(3)(c) lets regulations treat people as being OR as not being members of the same household, so "yes / no" is not enough.
DECLARE `s 39(3) what the regulations say about our household` IS ONE OF
    `s 39(3) the regulations treat us as members of the same household`
    `s 39(3) the regulations treat us as not members of the same household`
    `s 39(3) the regulations say nothing about it in our case`

-- s 39(3)
@export Are my partner and I a couple, once the regulations are applied?
GIVEN `we are married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and the other person married to each other or civil partners of each other?
      `we are members of the same household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and the other person members of the same household?
      `we are living together as if married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and the other person living together as if you were married or civil partners?
      `regulations disregard our marriage or civil partnership` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do the regulations say that your marriage or civil partnership is to be disregarded?
      `regulations treat us as living together as if married or civil partners` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do the regulations say that you are to be treated as living together as if married or civil partners?
      `what the regulations say about our household` IS A `s 39(3) what the regulations say about our household` @desc What do the regulations say about whether you are members of the same household?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 39(3), are the other person and I a couple once the regulations are applied` IS
    `s 39(3) the two people are a couple once the regulations supplied are applied`
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: the two of us` `we are married or civil partners` `we are members of the same household` `we are living together as if married or civil partners`)
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `regulations disregard our marriage or civil partnership`)
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `regulations treat us as living together as if married or civil partners`)
        (CONSIDER `what the regulations say about our household`
         WHEN `s 39(3) the regulations treat us as members of the same household` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 39(3) the regulations treat us as not members of the same household` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `s 39(3) the regulations say nothing about it in our case` THEN NOTHING)

-- s 40
@export Is this person a child?
GIVEN `their age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the person, in completed years?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 40, is this person a child` IS
    `s 40 the person is a child` (`s 1(1) seat helper: me` `their age in years` `England outside Greater London`)     -- placeholder place: s 40 does not read it

§ `Schedules 1 and 2 -- supplementary powers, and the amendments that bring in universal credit`

-- sch 1 para 4(5)
@export Does my joint claim count my own capital and income too?
GIVEN `we are joint claimants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming jointly with a partner?
      `regulations disregard my capital and income` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do the regulations say that your capital and income are to be disregarded in calculating our joint capital and income?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 4(5), does our joint capital and income include my separate capital and income` IS
    `sch 1 para 4(5) the joint capital and income includes this person's separate capital and income` `we are joint claimants` (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `regulations disregard my capital and income`)

-- sch 1 para 6(3)
@export Is this voucher for no more than the costs it covers?
GIVEN `the amount paid by means of the voucher` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is paid by means of the voucher?
      `the total of the amounts for those costs in my award` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the amounts in your award for the particular costs the voucher is for?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 6(3), is the amount paid by means of the voucher permitted` IS
    `sch 1 para 6(3) the amount paid by means of the voucher is permitted` `the amount paid by means of the voucher` `the total of the amounts for those costs in my award`

-- sch 1 para 7
@export Am I treated as outside the groups with fewer requirements because I have a right to reside?
GIVEN `I have a right to reside in the United Kingdom under the EU Treaties` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do you have a right to reside in the United Kingdom under the EU Treaties?
      `I would otherwise fall within section 19, 20 or 21` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Would you otherwise fall within section 19, 20 or 21?
      `regulations so provide` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do the regulations provide that such a claimant is to be treated as not falling within that section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 7, am I treated as not falling within section 19, 20 or 21` IS
    `sch 1 para 7 the claimant is treated as not falling within section 19, 20 or 21`
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `I have a right to reside in the United Kingdom under the EU Treaties`)
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `I would otherwise fall within section 19, 20 or 21`)
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `regulations so provide`)

-- sch 1 para 8(a)
@export Am I treated as having had a good reason?
GIVEN `I in fact had a good reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you in fact have a good reason for what you did or did not do?
      `regulations treat me as having or not having a good reason` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do the regulations say that you are to be treated as having (or not having) a good reason in your circumstances? (Answer "I do not know" if you are not aware of one.)
      `the regulations treat me as having one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the regulations apply to you: do they treat you as having a good reason? (No if they treat you as not having one.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 8(a), am I treated as having had a good reason` IS
    `sch 1 para 8(a) the person is treated as having a good reason for the act or omission` `I in fact had a good reason`
        (CONSIDER `regulations treat me as having or not having a good reason`
         WHEN `s 1(1) what I know: yes` THEN JUST `the regulations treat me as having one`
         OTHERWISE NOTHING)

-- sch 2, SSAA 159D(2)
@export How much universal credit is payable to me on a day after an alteration?
GIVEN `I have an award of universal credit in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an award of universal credit in force in your favour?
      `an alteration affects the amount I am entitled to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an alteration (in an element of universal credit, in your benefit income, in an amount deducted for earned income, or in a component of an allowance) affect the amount of universal credit you are entitled to?
      `an exception or condition applies to me` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Does an exception or condition that regulations prescribe take your case out of this rule?
      `my entitlement after the alteration` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of universal credit you are entitled to after the alteration?
      `the day the alteration comes into force for me` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the alteration come into force in relation to you?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 (section 159D(2) of the Social Security Administration Act 1992), what amount of universal credit is payable to me on the day` IS
    `sch 2 SSAA 159D(2) the amount of universal credit payable on the day without any further decision`
        `I have an award of universal credit in force` `an alteration affects the amount I am entitled to`
        (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `an exception or condition applies to me`)
        `my entitlement after the alteration` `the day the alteration comes into force for me` `the day I am asking about`

-- sch 2, SSAA 160C(2)
@export Is my increased amount of universal credit payable from the day I reach the age without any further decision?
GIVEN `I have an award of universal credit in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an award of universal credit in force in your favour?
      `an element applies because I or another person reached a particular age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an element of your award become applicable, or applicable at a particular rate, because you or another person reached a particular age?
      `I am entitled to an increased amount as a result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a result, are you entitled to an increased amount of universal credit?
      `a question arises about a Contributions and Benefits Act benefit or personal independence payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Because of reaching that age, does a question arise about your entitlement to a benefit under the Contributions and Benefits Act or to personal independence payment?
      `a question arises about universal credit other than the element or the variation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Because of reaching that age, does a question arise about your entitlement to universal credit, other than whether an element applies and whether the amount is to be varied?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 (section 160C(2) of the Social Security Administration Act 1992), is my increased amount payable from the day without any further decision` IS
    `sch 2 SSAA 160C(2) the increased amount is payable from the day without any further decision`
        `I have an award of universal credit in force` `an element applies because I or another person reached a particular age` `I am entitled to an increased amount as a result`
        `a question arises about a Contributions and Benefits Act benefit or personal independence payment`
        `a question arises about universal credit other than the element or the variation`

-- sch 2, SSA1998 Schedules 2 and 3
@export Is there a right of appeal against this decision about my benefit?
GIVEN decision IS A `sch 2 SSA1998 decision` @desc Which kind of decision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 (Schedules 2 and 3 to the Social Security Act 1998), does an appeal lie against this decision` IS
    `sch 2 SSA1998 an appeal lies against the decision` decision

-- sch 2, SPCA 4(1A)
@export Am I entitled to state pension credit if my partner is below the qualifying age?
GIVEN `I am a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a couple?
      `my partner has reached the qualifying age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the other member of the couple reached the qualifying age for state pension credit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 (section 4(1A) of the State Pension Credit Act 2002), am I entitled to state pension credit` IS
    `sch 2 SPCA 4(1A) the claimant is entitled to state pension credit` `I am a member of a couple` `my partner has reached the qualifying age`

-- sch 2, SSFA 6A(1)(za)
@export Is this benefit a disqualifying benefit under the Social Security Fraud Act 2001?
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit @desc Which benefit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 (section 6A(1) of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001), is this benefit a disqualifying benefit` IS
    `sch 2 SSFA 6A(1)(za) the benefit is a disqualifying benefit` benefit

-- sch 2: the host provisions that now include universal credit
@export Does this provision of another Act now include universal credit?
GIVEN provision IS A `sch 2 host provision` @desc Which provision of which Act?
      `the circumstances regulations prescribe apply to me` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc Do the circumstances that regulations prescribe for this provision apply to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2, does this host provision now include universal credit` IS
    `sch 2 the host provision now includes universal credit` provision (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `the circumstances regulations prescribe apply to me`)

§ `Schedules 5 and 6 -- working-age benefits together, and moving to universal credit`

-- sch 5 para 1(1)
@export Is this benefit a relevant benefit for the rules about dual entitlement?
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit @desc Which benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 1(1), is this benefit a relevant benefit` IS
    `sch 5 para 1(1) the benefit is a relevant benefit` benefit

-- sch 5 para 1(3)
@export Is this reduction a sanction for the rules about dual entitlement?
GIVEN reduction IS A `Provision that reduces an award` @desc Which provision reduces the award?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 1(3), is this reduction a sanction` IS
    `sch 5 para 1(3) the reduction is a sanction` reduction

-- sch 5 para 2(1)
@export How much of my other benefit is payable while I am also entitled to universal credit?
GIVEN `I am entitled to both` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to both the relevant benefit and universal credit?
      `the amount the regulations provide` IS A NUMBER @desc If the regulations give the amount payable, what is it? (Leave as 0 and answer "I do not know" below if they do not.)
      `I know the amount the regulations provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know the amount the regulations provide?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 2(1), what amount of the relevant benefit is payable to me` IS
    `sch 5 para 2(1) the amount payable by way of the relevant benefit` `I am entitled to both`
        (IF `I know the amount the regulations provide` THEN JUST `the amount the regulations provide` ELSE NOTHING)

-- sch 5 para 4
@export May regulations on hardship payments reach me if my award is reduced by the dual-entitlement regulations?
GIVEN `my award is reduced by regulations under paragraph 2(3)(b) or 3(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your award of universal credit reduced by regulations about the application of sanctions to a person entitled to both, or moving between, universal credit and another benefit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 4, may regulations under section 28 be made in relation to me` IS
    `sch 5 para 4 regulations under section 28 may be made in relation to the person` `my award is reduced by regulations under paragraph 2(3)(b) or 3(b)`

-- sch 6 para 1(1)
@export May regulations about moving me to universal credit include this provision?
GIVEN provision IS A `sch 6 provision regulations may include` @desc Which provision?
      `it is for the purposes of replacing existing benefits with universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision for the purposes of, or in connection with, replacing existing benefits with universal credit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6 paragraph 1(1), may the regulations include this provision` IS
    `sch 6 para 1(1) regulations may include this provision` provision `it is for the purposes of replacing existing benefits with universal credit`

-- sch 6 para 1(2)
@export Is my old benefit an existing benefit that universal credit replaces?
GIVEN `my old benefit` IS A Benefit @desc Which benefit did you receive before?
      `regulations prescribe it as an existing benefit` IS A `s 1(1) what I know` @desc If it is not one of the benefits abolished by section 33(1): do the regulations prescribe it as an existing benefit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6 paragraph 1(2), is my old benefit an existing benefit` IS
    `sch 6 para 1(2) the benefit is an existing benefit` `my old benefit` (`s 1(1) seat helper: what I know as yes, no or nothing` `regulations prescribe it as an existing benefit`)

-- sch 6 para 1(3)
@export Is this day the appointed day for universal credit?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `I know the day appointed for section 1 to come into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know the day appointed for section 1 (universal credit) to come into force?
      `the day appointed` IS A DATE @desc If you know it: which day was appointed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6 paragraph 1(3), is this day the appointed day` IS
    `sch 6 para 1(3) the day is the appointed day` `the day I am asking about`
        (IF `I know the day appointed for section 1 to come into force` THEN JUST `the day appointed` ELSE NOTHING)

-- sch 6 para 5(4)
@export Is this reduction a sanction for the rules about moving to universal credit?
GIVEN reduction IS A `Provision that reduces an award` @desc Which provision reduces the award?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6 paragraph 5(4), is this reduction a sanction` IS
    `sch 6 para 5(4) the reduction is a sanction` reduction

-- sch 6 para 5(4)
@export Is this benefit a relevant benefit for the rules about moving to universal credit?
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit @desc Which benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6 paragraph 5(4), is this benefit a relevant benefit` IS
    `sch 6 para 5(4) the benefit is a relevant benefit` benefit

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part wra2 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Welfare Reform Act 2012 (UK), 2012 c. 5, sections 44 to 76 and Schedules 3, 7 and 8 (part wra2) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who claims, receives or is moved to jobseeker's allowance, employment and support allowance or income support
-- (so also the person moved to universal credit from them), or who is asked about the other benefits these sections change.
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, a converter script's rendering; it is not the official text.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules of the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions that person asks. Nothing here is new law: each question
-- calls one or more layer-1 rules, building the records they take in a WHERE from the plain answers, and restates none of them.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.
-- Where the Act leaves a fact to regulations that are not among the sources (a prescribed circumstance, a prescribed amount, how the regulations
-- treat a good reason), the person answers "yes", "no" or "not known" (`Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer`), or gives the number
-- with a yes/no for "do you know it?"; a "not known" is passed to the layer-1 rule as NOTHING, and the answer then says so (it is NOTHING,
-- never FALSE). Layer-1 judgments the Act hands to someone else are not guessed here.
-- A question about a failure and its sanction only arises for a person who has failed to do something asked of them; the group headings say so.
--
-- Not asked here, with the reason in NOTES.md (Seat omissions): the layer-1 tables of repeals and lists (sections 60, 64, 68, 70, 73; Schedules 3 and 8),
-- the rules whose subject is an authority (the grant to a local authority in Schedule 3; the delegation in 11K/6L), and the rules that return a Person
-- (JSA 19(7), 19A(10), 19B(8)).
--
-- Seat names and constructors begin "Under ..." and are not shared with any other part.

DECLARE `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` IS ONE OF
    `Under wra2, yes`
    `Under wra2, no`
    `Under wra2, not known`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `Under wra2, yes` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Under wra2, no` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `Under wra2, not known` THEN NOTHING

GIVEN `the number` IS A NUMBER
      `the number is known` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under wra2, a number that may not be known` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number is known`
        THEN JUST `the number`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE
      `the date is known` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Under wra2, a date that may not be known` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date is known`
        THEN JUST `the date`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `Under section 57, how regulations treat my reason` IS ONE OF
    `Under section 57, regulations treat me as having a good reason`
    `Under section 57, regulations treat me as not having a good reason`
    `Under section 57, regulations do not treat my case`

GIVEN `the treatment` IS A `Under section 57, how regulations treat my reason`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 57, regulations' treatment as a three-valued fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the treatment`
    WHEN `Under section 57, regulations treat me as having a good reason` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Under section 57, regulations treat me as not having a good reason` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `Under section 57, regulations do not treat my case` THEN NOTHING

§ `Jobseeker's allowance: the claimant commitment (section 44)`

@export Under section 44, have I satisfied the condition of having accepted a claimant commitment (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 1(2)(b))?
GIVEN `I have accepted a claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you accepted a claimant commitment?
      `regulations treat me as having satisfied the condition` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Do regulations treat you, in your circumstances, as having satisfied the condition of accepting a claimant commitment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 44, have I satisfied the condition of having accepted a claimant commitment` IS
    `s 44(2) JSA 1(2)(b) the claimant satisfies the condition of having accepted a claimant commitment` `I have accepted a claimant commitment` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `regulations treat me as having satisfied the condition`)

@export Under section 44, have I accepted the claimant commitment (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 9(10))?
GIVEN `I accepted the most up-to-date version of the claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you accept the most up-to-date version of your claimant commitment?
      `I accepted it in the manner prescribed` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Did you accept it in the manner the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 44, have I accepted the claimant commitment` IS
    `s 44 JSA 9(10) the claimant accepts the claimant commitment` `I accepted the most up-to-date version of the claimant commitment` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `I accepted it in the manner prescribed`)

@export Under section 44, has the Secretary of State dealt with the reference about my claimant commitment in time (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 9(7)(a))?
GIVEN `the date the employment officer referred my proposed claimant commitment to the Secretary of State` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the employment officer refer your proposed claimant commitment to the Secretary of State?
      `the date the Secretary of State disposed of the reference` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Secretary of State dispose of the reference?
      `it was practicable to dispose of it within 14 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it practicable to dispose of the reference within 14 days of the date of the reference?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 44, has the Secretary of State dealt with the reference about my claimant commitment in time` IS
    `s 44 JSA 9(7)(a) the Secretary of State has disposed of the reference in time` `the date the employment officer referred my proposed claimant commitment to the Secretary of State` `the date the Secretary of State disposed of the reference` `it was practicable to dispose of it within 14 days`

@export Under section 44, on what date is my proposed claimant commitment treated as accepted (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 9(7)(c))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has directed that it is to be treated as accepted if conditions are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State directed that your proposed claimant commitment is to be treated as accepted if conditions are satisfied?
      `the conditions the direction sets are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions the direction sets satisfied?
      `I accepted it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you accept the proposed claimant commitment?
      `the date specified in the direction` IS A DATE @desc What date does the direction specify?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 44, on what date is my proposed claimant commitment treated as accepted` IS
    `s 44 JSA 9(7)(c) the date on which the proposed claimant commitment is treated as accepted` `the Secretary of State has directed that it is to be treated as accepted if conditions are satisfied` `the conditions the direction sets are satisfied` `I accepted it` `the date specified in the direction`

@export Under section 44, may this person vary my claimant commitment (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 10(1))?
GIVEN `the person who would vary my claimant commitment` IS A Authority @desc Who would vary your claimant commitment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 44, may this person vary my claimant commitment` IS
    `s 44 JSA 10(1) the claimant commitment may be varied by that person` `the person who would vary my claimant commitment`

@export Under section 44, was I notified before my claimant commitment was varied (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 10(3))?
GIVEN `the variation relates to information about the conditions in section 1(2)(a) and (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the variation relate to information in your claimant commitment about being available for and actively seeking work?
      `I was notified of the proposed variation before it was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you told of the proposed variation before it was made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 44, was I notified before my claimant commitment was varied` IS
    `s 44 JSA 10(3) the employment officer has notified the claimant before making the variation` `the variation relates to information about the conditions in section 1(2)(a) and (c)` `I was notified of the proposed variation before it was made`

§ `Jobseeker's allowance: sanctions in the interim period (section 46)`
-- This group only arises for a person whose jobseeker's allowance may be reduced for a failure (the form can ask 'Has this happened to you?' before showing it).

@export Under section 46, is my failure sanctionable under section 19 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 19(2))?
GIVEN `I lost my employment through misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you lose your employment as an employed earner through misconduct?
      `I voluntarily left my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you voluntarily leave your employment as an employed earner?
      `I refused or failed to apply for, or accept, a vacancy an employment officer told me of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse or fail to apply for, or accept if offered, a job an employment officer told you was vacant or about to become vacant?
      `I neglected to avail myself of a reasonable opportunity of employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you neglect to take a reasonable opportunity of employment?
      `I failed to participate in a prescribed scheme within section 17A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to participate in a prescribed employment scheme?
      `I had a good reason on the facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a good reason for what you did or did not do?
      `regulations treat my case as to a good reason` IS A `s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA regulations' treatment of a good reason` @desc How do the regulations treat your case as to whether you had a good reason?
      `regulations treat me as not having left voluntarily` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Do regulations treat you as not having left your employment voluntarily (for example after volunteering for redundancy)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 46, is my failure sanctionable under section 19 of the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS
    `my failure is sanctionable`
    WHERE
        `my failure` MEANS `s 46 JSA 19(2) failure` WITH
            `through misconduct the claimant loses employment as an employed earner` IS `I lost my employment through misconduct`
            `the claimant voluntarily leaves such employment` IS `I voluntarily left my employment`
            `the claimant refuses or fails to apply for, or accept if offered, a situation in employment that an employment officer has informed the claimant is vacant or about to become vacant` IS `I refused or failed to apply for, or accept, a vacancy an employment officer told me of`
            `the claimant neglects to avail of a reasonable opportunity of employment` IS `I neglected to avail myself of a reasonable opportunity of employment`
            `the claimant fails to participate in a scheme within section 17A(1) prescribed for the purposes of section 19` IS `I failed to participate in a prescribed scheme within section 17A(1)`
        `my good reason` MEANS (`s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA(a) the claimant has a good reason for the act or omission` `I had a good reason on the facts` (JUST `regulations treat my case as to a good reason`))
        `my failure is sanctionable` MEANS `s 46 JSA 19(2) the failure is sanctionable under section 19` `my failure` `my good reason` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `regulations treat me as not having left voluntarily`)

@export Under section 46, is my award to be reduced under section 19 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 19(1))?
GIVEN `I lost my employment through misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you lose your employment as an employed earner through misconduct?
      `I voluntarily left my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you voluntarily leave your employment as an employed earner?
      `I refused or failed to apply for, or accept, a vacancy an employment officer told me of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse or fail to apply for, or accept if offered, a job an employment officer told you was vacant or about to become vacant?
      `I neglected to avail myself of a reasonable opportunity of employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you neglect to take a reasonable opportunity of employment?
      `I failed to participate in a prescribed scheme within section 17A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to participate in a prescribed employment scheme?
      `I had a good reason on the facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a good reason for what you did or did not do?
      `regulations treat my case as to a good reason` IS A `s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA regulations' treatment of a good reason` @desc How do the regulations treat your case as to whether you had a good reason?
      `regulations treat me as not having left voluntarily` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Do regulations treat you as not having left your employment voluntarily (for example after volunteering for redundancy)?
      `regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in my case` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Do regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 46, is my award to be reduced under section 19 of the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS
    `s 46 JSA 19(1) the award is to be reduced in accordance with section 19` `my failure is sanctionable` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in my case`)
    WHERE
        `my failure` MEANS `s 46 JSA 19(2) failure` WITH
            `through misconduct the claimant loses employment as an employed earner` IS `I lost my employment through misconduct`
            `the claimant voluntarily leaves such employment` IS `I voluntarily left my employment`
            `the claimant refuses or fails to apply for, or accept if offered, a situation in employment that an employment officer has informed the claimant is vacant or about to become vacant` IS `I refused or failed to apply for, or accept, a vacancy an employment officer told me of`
            `the claimant neglects to avail of a reasonable opportunity of employment` IS `I neglected to avail myself of a reasonable opportunity of employment`
            `the claimant fails to participate in a scheme within section 17A(1) prescribed for the purposes of section 19` IS `I failed to participate in a prescribed scheme within section 17A(1)`
        `my good reason` MEANS (`s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA(a) the claimant has a good reason for the act or omission` `I had a good reason on the facts` (JUST `regulations treat my case as to a good reason`))
        `my failure is sanctionable` MEANS `s 46 JSA 19(2) the failure is sanctionable under section 19` `my failure` `my good reason` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `regulations treat me as not having left voluntarily`)

@export Under section 46, is my failure sanctionable under section 19A of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 19A(2) and (3))?
GIVEN `I failed to comply with regulations under section 8(1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with regulations about attending and signing on?
      `I failed to comply with regulations under section 17A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with regulations about an employment scheme?
      `I refused or failed to carry out a reasonable jobseeker's direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse or fail to carry out a jobseeker's direction that was reasonable having regard to your circumstances?
      `I neglected a reasonable opportunity of a place on a training scheme or employment programme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you neglect to take a reasonable opportunity of a place on a training scheme or employment programme?
      `I refused or failed to apply for, or accept, a place an employment officer told me of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse or fail to apply for, or accept if offered, a place on such a scheme that an employment officer told you was vacant?
      `I gave up a place or failed to attend it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give up a place on such a scheme or programme, or fail to attend it having been given a place?
      `I lost a place through misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you lose a place on such a scheme or programme through misconduct?
      `I had a good reason on the facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a good reason for what you did or did not do?
      `regulations treat my case as to a good reason` IS A `s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA regulations' treatment of a good reason` @desc How do the regulations treat your case as to whether you had a good reason?
      `my failure is also sanctionable under section 19` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Is your failure also sanctionable under section 19 (a higher-level sanction)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 46, is my failure sanctionable under section 19A of the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS
    `my failure is sanctionable`
    WHERE
        `my failure` MEANS `s 46 JSA 19A(2) failure` WITH
            `the claimant fails to comply with regulations under section 8(1) or (1A)` IS `I failed to comply with regulations under section 8(1) or (1A)`
            `the claimant fails to comply with regulations under section 17A` IS `I failed to comply with regulations under section 17A`
            `the claimant refuses or fails to carry out a jobseeker's direction that was reasonable having regard to the claimant's circumstances` IS `I refused or failed to carry out a reasonable jobseeker's direction`
            `the claimant neglects to avail of a reasonable opportunity of a place on a training scheme or employment programme` IS `I neglected a reasonable opportunity of a place on a training scheme or employment programme`
            `the claimant refuses or fails to apply for, or accept if offered, a place on such a scheme or programme that an employment officer has informed the claimant is vacant or about to become vacant` IS `I refused or failed to apply for, or accept, a place an employment officer told me of`
            `the claimant gives up a place on such a scheme or programme or fails to attend it having been given a place` IS `I gave up a place or failed to attend it`
            `through misconduct the claimant loses a place on such a scheme or programme` IS `I lost a place through misconduct`
        `my good reason` MEANS (`s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA(a) the claimant has a good reason for the act or omission` `I had a good reason on the facts` (JUST `regulations treat my case as to a good reason`))
        `my failure is sanctionable` MEANS `s 46 JSA 19A(3) the failure is sanctionable under section 19A` (`s 46 JSA 19A(2) the failure is of a kind that section 19A(2) makes sanctionable` `my failure` `my good reason`) (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `my failure is also sanctionable under section 19`)

@export Under section 46, is my award to be reduced under section 19A of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 19A(1))?
GIVEN `I failed to comply with regulations under section 8(1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with regulations about attending and signing on?
      `I failed to comply with regulations under section 17A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with regulations about an employment scheme?
      `I refused or failed to carry out a reasonable jobseeker's direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse or fail to carry out a jobseeker's direction that was reasonable having regard to your circumstances?
      `I neglected a reasonable opportunity of a place on a training scheme or employment programme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you neglect to take a reasonable opportunity of a place on a training scheme or employment programme?
      `I refused or failed to apply for, or accept, a place an employment officer told me of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse or fail to apply for, or accept if offered, a place on such a scheme that an employment officer told you was vacant?
      `I gave up a place or failed to attend it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give up a place on such a scheme or programme, or fail to attend it having been given a place?
      `I lost a place through misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you lose a place on such a scheme or programme through misconduct?
      `I had a good reason on the facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a good reason for what you did or did not do?
      `regulations treat my case as to a good reason` IS A `s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA regulations' treatment of a good reason` @desc How do the regulations treat your case as to whether you had a good reason?
      `my failure is also sanctionable under section 19` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Is your failure also sanctionable under section 19 (a higher-level sanction)?
      `regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in my case` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Do regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 46, is my award to be reduced under section 19A of the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS
    `s 46 JSA 19A(1) the award is to be reduced in accordance with section 19A` `my failure is sanctionable` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in my case`)
    WHERE
        `my failure` MEANS `s 46 JSA 19A(2) failure` WITH
            `the claimant fails to comply with regulations under section 8(1) or (1A)` IS `I failed to comply with regulations under section 8(1) or (1A)`
            `the claimant fails to comply with regulations under section 17A` IS `I failed to comply with regulations under section 17A`
            `the claimant refuses or fails to carry out a jobseeker's direction that was reasonable having regard to the claimant's circumstances` IS `I refused or failed to carry out a reasonable jobseeker's direction`
            `the claimant neglects to avail of a reasonable opportunity of a place on a training scheme or employment programme` IS `I neglected a reasonable opportunity of a place on a training scheme or employment programme`
            `the claimant refuses or fails to apply for, or accept if offered, a place on such a scheme or programme that an employment officer has informed the claimant is vacant or about to become vacant` IS `I refused or failed to apply for, or accept, a place an employment officer told me of`
            `the claimant gives up a place on such a scheme or programme or fails to attend it having been given a place` IS `I gave up a place or failed to attend it`
            `through misconduct the claimant loses a place on such a scheme or programme` IS `I lost a place through misconduct`
        `my good reason` MEANS (`s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA(a) the claimant has a good reason for the act or omission` `I had a good reason on the facts` (JUST `regulations treat my case as to a good reason`))
        `my failure is sanctionable` MEANS `s 46 JSA 19A(3) the failure is sanctionable under section 19A` (`s 46 JSA 19A(2) the failure is of a kind that section 19A(2) makes sanctionable` `my failure` `my good reason`) (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `my failure is also sanctionable under section 19`)

@export Under section 46, is the period of my higher-level reduction within three years (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 19(4)(b))?
GIVEN `the first day of the reduction` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the reduction?
      `the last day of the reduction` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the reduction?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 46, is the period of my higher-level reduction within three years` IS
    `s 46 JSA 19(4)(b) the period of the reduction is within three years` `the first day of the reduction` `the last day of the reduction`

@export Under section 46, is the fixed period of my other reduction within 26 weeks (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 19A(5)(b))?
GIVEN `the first day of the reduction` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the reduction?
      `the last day of the reduction` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the reduction?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 46, is the fixed period of my other reduction within 26 weeks` IS
    `s 46 JSA 19A(5)(b) the fixed period of the reduction is within 26 weeks` `the first day of the reduction` `the last day of the reduction`

@export Under section 46, how much will my award be after the reduction (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 19(4)(a))?
GIVEN `the award before the reduction, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your award before the reduction, in pounds?
      `the reduction the regulations specify, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What reduction do the regulations specify, in pounds? (0 if you do not know)
      `I know the reduction the regulations specify` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know the reduction the regulations specify?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 46, how much will my award be after the reduction` IS
    `s 46 JSA 19(4)(a) the award after the reduction, in pounds` `the award before the reduction, in pounds` (`Under wra2, a number that may not be known` `the reduction the regulations specify, in pounds` `I know the reduction the regulations specify`)

@export Under section 46, may regulations provide for hardship payments to me (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 19C(1))?
GIVEN `my award is reduced under sections 19 to 19B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your award reduced under section 19, 19A or 19B?
      `I am or will be in hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or will you be, in hardship?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 46, may regulations provide for hardship payments to me` IS
    `s 46 JSA 19C(1) regulations may provide for hardship payments to the claimant` `my award is reduced under sections 19 to 19B` `I am or will be in hardship`

§ `Jobseeker's allowance: work-related requirements and sanctions after universal credit (section 49)`
-- The sanction questions in this group only arise for a person who failed to do something asked of them (the form can ask 'Has this happened to you?' first).

@export Under section 49, may the Secretary of State require me to take part in an interview for this purpose (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 6G(1))?
GIVEN `the purpose of the interview` IS A `s 49 JSA 6G(1) purpose of an interview` @desc What is the purpose of the interview?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 49, may the Secretary of State require me to take part in an interview for this purpose` IS
    `s 49 JSA 6G(1) the Secretary of State may require the claimant to participate in an interview for that purpose` `the purpose of the interview`

@export Under section 49, may the Secretary of State require me to report this change in my circumstances (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 6G(4))?
GIVEN `the change is relevant to the imposition of work-related requirements on me, or to my compliance with one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change relevant to the work-related requirements imposed on you, or to your compliance with one?
      `the change has been specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this kind of change been specified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 49, may the Secretary of State require me to report this change in my circumstances` IS
    `s 49 JSA 6G(4) the Secretary of State may require the claimant to report the change in circumstances` `the change is relevant to the imposition of work-related requirements on me, or to my compliance with one` `the change has been specified`

@export Under section 49, does a requirement imposed on me cease to have effect for 13 weeks (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 6H(5))?
GIVEN `I have recently been a victim of domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you recently been a victim of domestic violence?
      `I am in the circumstances the regulations prescribe` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Are you in the circumstances the regulations prescribe for this protection?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 49, does a requirement imposed on me cease to have effect for 13 weeks` IS
    `s 49 JSA 6H(5) a requirement imposed on the claimant ceases to have effect for 13 weeks` `I have recently been a victim of domestic violence` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `I am in the circumstances the regulations prescribe`)

@export Under section 49, on what day do the 13 weeks of protection end (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 6H(5)(a))?
GIVEN `the first day on which the requirement ceases to have effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the requirement first cease to have effect?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 49, on what day do the 13 weeks of protection end` IS
    `s 49 JSA 6H(5)(a) the last day of the period of 13 weeks` `the first day on which the requirement ceases to have effect`

@export Under section 49, is my failure sanctionable under section 6J of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 6J(2))?
GIVEN `I failed to comply with a requirement to undertake a work placement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with a requirement to undertake a work placement?
      `the work placement was of a prescribed description` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Was the work placement of a description the regulations prescribe?
      `I failed to comply with a requirement to apply for a particular vacancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with a requirement to apply for a particular vacancy for paid work?
      `I failed to take up an offer of paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to take up an offer of paid work, in breach of a work availability requirement?
      `I ceased paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease paid work?
      `I lost pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you lose pay?
      `regulations treat it as misconduct` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Do regulations treat what happened as misconduct?
      `regulations treat it as voluntary` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Do regulations treat what happened as voluntary?
      `the loss of pay was below the prescribed level` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Was the loss of pay below the level the regulations prescribe?
      `I had a good reason on the facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a good reason for what you did or did not do?
      `regulations treat my case as to a good reason` IS A `s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA regulations' treatment of a good reason` @desc How do the regulations treat your case as to whether you had a good reason?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 49, is my failure sanctionable under section 6J of the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS
    `my failure is sanctionable`
    WHERE
        `my good reason` MEANS (`s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA(a) the claimant has a good reason for the act or omission` `I had a good reason on the facts` (JUST `regulations treat my case as to a good reason`))
        `my failure` MEANS `s 49 JSA 6J(2) failure` WITH
            `the claimant failed to comply with a requirement under a work preparation requirement to undertake a work placement` IS `I failed to comply with a requirement to undertake a work placement`
            `the work placement was of a prescribed description` IS (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `the work placement was of a prescribed description`)
            `the claimant failed to comply with a requirement under a work search requirement to apply for a particular vacancy for paid work` IS `I failed to comply with a requirement to apply for a particular vacancy`
            `the claimant failed to comply with a work availability requirement by not taking up an offer of paid work` IS `I failed to take up an offer of paid work`
            `the claimant ceased paid work or lost pay in a way that counts under paragraph (d)` IS `s 49 JSA 6J(2)(d) the claimant ceased paid work or lost pay in a way that counts` `I ceased paid work` `I lost pay` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `regulations treat it as misconduct`) (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `regulations treat it as voluntary`) `my good reason` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `the loss of pay was below the prescribed level`)
        `my failure is sanctionable` MEANS `s 49 JSA 6J(2) the failure is sanctionable under section 6J` `my failure` `my good reason`

@export Under section 49, is my award to be reduced under section 6J of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 6J(1))?
GIVEN `I failed to comply with a requirement to undertake a work placement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with a requirement to undertake a work placement?
      `the work placement was of a prescribed description` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Was the work placement of a description the regulations prescribe?
      `I failed to comply with a requirement to apply for a particular vacancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with a requirement to apply for a particular vacancy for paid work?
      `I failed to take up an offer of paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to take up an offer of paid work, in breach of a work availability requirement?
      `I ceased paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease paid work?
      `I lost pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you lose pay?
      `regulations treat it as misconduct` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Do regulations treat what happened as misconduct?
      `regulations treat it as voluntary` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Do regulations treat what happened as voluntary?
      `the loss of pay was below the prescribed level` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Was the loss of pay below the level the regulations prescribe?
      `I had a good reason on the facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a good reason for what you did or did not do?
      `regulations treat my case as to a good reason` IS A `s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA regulations' treatment of a good reason` @desc How do the regulations treat your case as to whether you had a good reason?
      `regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in my case` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Do regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 49, is my award to be reduced under section 6J of the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS
    `s 49 JSA 6J(1) the award is to be reduced in accordance with section 6J` `my failure is sanctionable` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in my case`)
    WHERE
        `my good reason` MEANS (`s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA(a) the claimant has a good reason for the act or omission` `I had a good reason on the facts` (JUST `regulations treat my case as to a good reason`))
        `my failure` MEANS `s 49 JSA 6J(2) failure` WITH
            `the claimant failed to comply with a requirement under a work preparation requirement to undertake a work placement` IS `I failed to comply with a requirement to undertake a work placement`
            `the work placement was of a prescribed description` IS (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `the work placement was of a prescribed description`)
            `the claimant failed to comply with a requirement under a work search requirement to apply for a particular vacancy for paid work` IS `I failed to comply with a requirement to apply for a particular vacancy`
            `the claimant failed to comply with a work availability requirement by not taking up an offer of paid work` IS `I failed to take up an offer of paid work`
            `the claimant ceased paid work or lost pay in a way that counts under paragraph (d)` IS `s 49 JSA 6J(2)(d) the claimant ceased paid work or lost pay in a way that counts` `I ceased paid work` `I lost pay` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `regulations treat it as misconduct`) (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `regulations treat it as voluntary`) `my good reason` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `the loss of pay was below the prescribed level`)
        `my failure is sanctionable` MEANS `s 49 JSA 6J(2) the failure is sanctionable under section 6J` `my failure` `my good reason`

@export Under section 49, is my failure sanctionable under section 6K of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 6K(2) and (3))?
GIVEN `I failed to comply with a work-related requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with a work-related requirement?
      `I failed to comply with a requirement under section 6G` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with a requirement to attend an interview, provide information or report a change?
      `I had a good reason on the facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a good reason for what you did or did not do?
      `regulations treat my case as to a good reason` IS A `s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA regulations' treatment of a good reason` @desc How do the regulations treat your case as to whether you had a good reason?
      `my failure is also sanctionable under section 6J` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Is your failure also sanctionable under section 6J (a higher-level sanction)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 49, is my failure sanctionable under section 6K of the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS
    `s 49 JSA 6K(3) the failure is sanctionable under section 6K` (`s 49 JSA 6K(2) the failure is of a kind that section 6K(2) makes sanctionable` `I failed to comply with a work-related requirement` `I failed to comply with a requirement under section 6G` `my good reason`) (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `my failure is also sanctionable under section 6J`)
    WHERE
        `my good reason` MEANS (`s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA(a) the claimant has a good reason for the act or omission` `I had a good reason on the facts` (JUST `regulations treat my case as to a good reason`))

@export Under section 49, is my award to be reduced under section 6K of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 6K(1))?
GIVEN `I failed to comply with a work-related requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with a work-related requirement?
      `I failed to comply with a requirement under section 6G` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with a requirement to attend an interview, provide information or report a change?
      `I had a good reason on the facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a good reason for what you did or did not do?
      `regulations treat my case as to a good reason` IS A `s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA regulations' treatment of a good reason` @desc How do the regulations treat your case as to whether you had a good reason?
      `my failure is also sanctionable under section 6J` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Is your failure also sanctionable under section 6J (a higher-level sanction)?
      `regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in my case` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Do regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 49, is my award to be reduced under section 6K of the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS
    `s 49 JSA 6K(1) the award is to be reduced in accordance with section 6K` (`s 49 JSA 6K(3) the failure is sanctionable under section 6K` (`s 49 JSA 6K(2) the failure is of a kind that section 6K(2) makes sanctionable` `I failed to comply with a work-related requirement` `I failed to comply with a requirement under section 6G` `my good reason`) (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `my failure is also sanctionable under section 6J`)) (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in my case`)
    WHERE
        `my good reason` MEANS (`s 46(3) JSA Sch 1 para 14AA(a) the claimant has a good reason for the act or omission` `I had a good reason on the facts` (JUST `regulations treat my case as to a good reason`))

@export Under section 49, is the period of my higher-level reduction within three years (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 6J(5)(b))?
GIVEN `the first day of the reduction` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the reduction?
      `the last day of the reduction` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the reduction?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 49, is the period of my higher-level reduction within three years` IS
    `s 49 JSA 6J(5)(b) the period of the reduction is within three years` `the first day of the reduction` `the last day of the reduction`

@export Under section 49, is the fixed period of my other reduction within 26 weeks (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 6K(5)(b))?
GIVEN `the first day of the reduction` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the reduction?
      `the last day of the reduction` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the reduction?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 49, is the fixed period of my other reduction within 26 weeks` IS
    `s 49 JSA 6K(5)(b) the fixed period of the reduction is within 26 weeks` `the first day of the reduction` `the last day of the reduction`

@export Under section 49, how much will my award be after the higher-level reduction (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 6J(5)(a))?
GIVEN `the award before the reduction, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your award before the reduction, in pounds?
      `the reduction the regulations specify, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What reduction do the regulations specify, in pounds? (0 if you do not know)
      `I know the reduction the regulations specify` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know the reduction the regulations specify?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 49, how much will my award be after the higher-level reduction` IS
    `s 49 JSA 6J(5)(a) the award after the reduction, in pounds` `the award before the reduction, in pounds` (`Under wra2, a number that may not be known` `the reduction the regulations specify, in pounds` `I know the reduction the regulations specify`)

§ `Employment and support allowance: entitlement and the claimant commitment (sections 50 to 56)`

@export Under section 50, is my couple within the reference to a couple entitled to a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance (Welfare Reform Act 2007, section 1(6A))?
GIVEN `my allowance is a contributory allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your allowance a contributory employment and support allowance?
      `my couple is entitled to a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your couple entitled to a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance?
      `my couple is so entitled by virtue of regulations under paragraph 8A of Schedule 1 to the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your couple so entitled by virtue of regulations under paragraph 8A of Schedule 1 to the Jobseekers Act 1995?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 50, is my couple within the reference to a couple entitled to a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance` IS
    `s 50(1) WRA2007 1(6A) the couple is within the reference in subsection (3)(f)` `my allowance is a contributory allowance` `my couple is entitled to a joint-claim jobseeker's allowance` `my couple is so entitled by virtue of regulations under paragraph 8A of Schedule 1 to the Jobseekers Act 1995`

@export Under section 51, is my period of entitlement within the relevant maximum number of days (Welfare Reform Act 2007, section 1A(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `the days I am entitled by virtue of the first and second conditions` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of contributory allowance have you been entitled to by virtue of the first and second conditions, counting days before and after the section came into force, and leaving out the days section 1A(5) excludes?
      `the greater number of days an order specifies` IS A NUMBER @desc What greater number of days does an order made by the Secretary of State specify? (0 if there is none)
      `there is such an order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State made an order specifying a greater number of days?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 51, is my period of entitlement within the relevant maximum number of days` IS
    `s 51 WRA2007 1A(1) the period of entitlement is within the relevant maximum` `the days I am entitled by virtue of the first and second conditions` (`s 51 WRA2007 1A(2) the relevant maximum number of days` (`Under wra2, a number that may not be known` `the greater number of days an order specifies` `there is such an order`))

@export Under section 51, how many days of my entitlement are counted (Welfare Reform Act 2007, section 1A(5) and (6))?
GIVEN `the days of entitlement before section 51 came into force` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days were you entitled to the allowance before the section came into force?
      `the days of entitlement after section 51 came into force` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have you been entitled to the allowance since the section came into force?
      `the days on which I am a member of the support group` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those days were days on which you were a member of the support group?
      `the other days on which I am entitled to the support component` IS A NUMBER @desc How many other days were days on which you were entitled to the support component?
      `the assessment phase days that lead into the support group or the support component` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days in the assessment phase were followed immediately by days in the support group or days of entitlement to the support component?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 51, how many days of my entitlement are counted` IS
    `s 51 WRA2007 1A(5) the days that are counted` (`s 51 WRA2007 1A(6) the days of entitlement that are counted before the exclusions in subsection (5)` `the days of entitlement before section 51 came into force` `the days of entitlement after section 51 came into force`) `the days on which I am a member of the support group` `the other days on which I am entitled to the support component` `the assessment phase days that lead into the support group or the support component`

@export Under section 52, am I entitled to an employment and support allowance by virtue of section 1B (Welfare Reform Act 2007, section 1B(1))?
GIVEN `my entitlement to a contributory allowance ceased as a result of section 1A(1) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your entitlement to a contributory allowance cease because of the time limit in section 1A?
      `I have not since ceased to have limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you continued to have (or be treated as having) limited capability for work since then?
      `I satisfy the basic conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the basic conditions of entitlement?
      `I have limited capability for work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have (or are you treated as having) limited capability for work-related activity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 52, am I entitled to an employment and support allowance by virtue of section 1B` IS
    `s 52 WRA2007 1B(1) the claimant is entitled to an employment and support allowance by virtue of section 1B` `my entitlement to a contributory allowance ceased as a result of section 1A(1) or (4)` `I have not since ceased to have limited capability for work` `I satisfy the basic conditions` `I have limited capability for work-related activity`

@export Under section 53, may a claim be made for an employment and support allowance by virtue of the third condition (Welfare Reform Act 2007, section 1(3A))?
GIVEN `the claim is by virtue of the third condition (youth)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim made by virtue of the third condition (youth)?
      `the date of the claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the claim made?
      `the date on which subsection (3A) came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what date did subsection (3A) come into force? (any date if you do not know)
      `I know the date on which subsection (3A) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know the date on which subsection (3A) came into force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 53, may a claim be made for an employment and support allowance by virtue of the third condition` IS
    `s 53 WRA2007 1(3A) a claim may be made by virtue of the third condition` `the claim is by virtue of the third condition (youth)` `the date of the claim` (`Under wra2, a date that may not be known` `the date on which subsection (3A) came into force` `I know the date on which subsection (3A) came into force`)

@export Under section 54, have I satisfied the condition of having accepted a claimant commitment for employment and support allowance (Welfare Reform Act 2007, section 1(3)(aa))?
GIVEN `I have accepted a claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you accepted a claimant commitment?
      `regulations treat me as having satisfied the condition` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Do regulations treat you, in your circumstances, as having satisfied the condition of accepting a claimant commitment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 54, have I satisfied the condition of having accepted a claimant commitment for employment and support allowance` IS
    `s 54(2) WRA2007 1(3)(aa) the claimant satisfies the condition of having accepted a claimant commitment` `I have accepted a claimant commitment` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `regulations treat me as having satisfied the condition`)

@export Under section 54, have I accepted the claimant commitment for employment and support allowance (Welfare Reform Act 2007, section 1C(5))?
GIVEN `I accepted the most up-to-date version of the claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you accept the most up-to-date version of your claimant commitment?
      `I accepted it in the manner prescribed` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Did you accept it in the manner the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 54, have I accepted the claimant commitment for employment and support allowance` IS
    `s 54 WRA2007 1C(5) the claimant accepts the claimant commitment` `I accepted the most up-to-date version of the claimant commitment` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `I accepted it in the manner prescribed`)

@export Under section 56, may regulations provide for hardship payments to me while my employment and support allowance is reduced (Welfare Reform Act 2007, section 16A(1))?
GIVEN `my allowance is reduced by virtue of regulations under section 11(3), 12(3) or 13(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount of your allowance reduced by virtue of regulations about work-related requirements?
      `I am or will be in hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or will you be, in hardship?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 56, may regulations provide for hardship payments to me while my employment and support allowance is reduced` IS
    `s 56 WRA2007 16A(1) regulations may provide for hardship payments to the person` `my allowance is reduced by virtue of regulations under section 11(3), 12(3) or 13(3)` `I am or will be in hardship`

§ `Employment and support allowance: work-related requirements and sanctions (section 57)`
-- The sanction questions in this group only arise for a person who failed to do something asked of them (the form can ask 'Has this happened to you?' first).

@export Under section 57, may the Secretary of State impose a work-related requirement on me (Welfare Reform Act 2007, sections 11D(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `I have limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have limited capability for work and work-related activity?
      `my responsibilities are regular and substantial caring responsibilities as regulations prescribe` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Do you have regular and substantial caring responsibilities, as the regulations define them?
      `the person I care for is severely disabled as regulations prescribe` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Is the person you care for severely disabled, as the regulations define it?
      `s 39(1) the person is a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a couple?
      `I am responsible for the child, as the circumstances regulations specify` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Are you responsible for the child, in the circumstances the regulations specify?
      `the age of the child in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the child, in completed years?
      `I am of a description prescribed for section 11D(2)(d)` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Are you of a description the regulations prescribe for section 11D(2)(d)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 57, may the Secretary of State impose a work-related requirement on me` IS
    `s 57 WRA2007 11D(1) the Secretary of State may impose a work-related requirement on the person` (`s 57 WRA2007 11D(2) the person falls within section 11D` `I have limited capability for work and work-related activity` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `my responsibilities are regular and substantial caring responsibilities as regulations prescribe`) (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `the person I care for is severely disabled as regulations prescribe`) `s 39(1) the person is a member of a couple` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `I am responsible for the child, as the circumstances regulations specify`) `the age of the child in years` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `I am of a description prescribed for section 11D(2)(d)`))

@export Under section 57, may the Secretary of State impose a work preparation requirement on me (Welfare Reform Act 2007, sections 11E(1) and (3))?
GIVEN `s 39(1) the person is a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a couple?
      `I am responsible for the child, as the circumstances regulations specify` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Are you responsible for the child, in the circumstances the regulations specify?
      `the age of the child in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the child, in completed years?
      `the age that regulations prescribe` IS A NUMBER @desc What age do the regulations prescribe for section 11E(1)(a)? (0 if you do not know)
      `I know the age that regulations prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know the age the regulations prescribe?
      `I am of a description prescribed for section 11E(1)(b)` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Are you of a description the regulations prescribe for section 11E(1)(b)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 57, may the Secretary of State impose a work preparation requirement on me` IS
    `s 57 WRA2007 11E(3) the Secretary of State may impose a work preparation requirement` (`s 57 WRA2007 11E(1) the person falls within section 11E` `s 39(1) the person is a member of a couple` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `I am responsible for the child, as the circumstances regulations specify`) `the age of the child in years` (`Under wra2, a number that may not be known` `the age that regulations prescribe` `I know the age that regulations prescribe`) (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `I am of a description prescribed for section 11E(1)(b)`))

@export Under section 57, may the Secretary of State impose a work-focused interview requirement on me (Welfare Reform Act 2007, section 11E(2))?
GIVEN `I am entitled to an employment and support allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to an employment and support allowance?
      `s 39(1) the person is a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a couple?
      `I am responsible for the child, as the circumstances regulations specify` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Are you responsible for the child, in the circumstances the regulations specify?
      `the age of the child in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the child, in completed years?
      `the age that regulations prescribe` IS A NUMBER @desc What age do the regulations prescribe for section 11E(1)(a)? (0 if you do not know)
      `I know the age that regulations prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know the age the regulations prescribe?
      `I am of a description prescribed for section 11E(1)(b)` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Are you of a description the regulations prescribe for section 11E(1)(b)?
      `another provision of this Part limits the imposition` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Does another provision of the same Part of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 limit the imposition of a work-focused interview requirement on you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 57, may the Secretary of State impose a work-focused interview requirement on me` IS
    `s 57 WRA2007 11E(2) the Secretary of State may impose a work-focused interview requirement` `I am entitled to an employment and support allowance` (`s 57 WRA2007 11E(1) the person falls within section 11E` `s 39(1) the person is a member of a couple` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `I am responsible for the child, as the circumstances regulations specify`) `the age of the child in years` (`Under wra2, a number that may not be known` `the age that regulations prescribe` `I know the age that regulations prescribe`) (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `I am of a description prescribed for section 11E(1)(b)`)) (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `another provision of this Part limits the imposition`)

@export Under section 57, which group of work-related requirements am I in (Welfare Reform Act 2007, section 11(3))?
GIVEN `I have limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have limited capability for work and work-related activity?
      `my responsibilities are regular and substantial caring responsibilities as regulations prescribe` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Do you have regular and substantial caring responsibilities, as the regulations define them?
      `the person I care for is severely disabled as regulations prescribe` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Is the person you care for severely disabled, as the regulations define it?
      `s 39(1) the person is a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a couple?
      `I am responsible for the child, as the circumstances regulations specify` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Are you responsible for the child, in the circumstances the regulations specify?
      `the age of the child in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the child, in completed years?
      `I am of a description prescribed for section 11D(2)(d)` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Are you of a description the regulations prescribe for section 11D(2)(d)?
      `the age that regulations prescribe` IS A NUMBER @desc What age do the regulations prescribe for section 11E(1)(a)? (0 if you do not know)
      `I know the age that regulations prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know the age the regulations prescribe?
      `I am of a description prescribed for section 11E(1)(b)` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Are you of a description the regulations prescribe for section 11E(1)(b)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 57 WRA2007 11(3) group`
DECIDE `Under section 57, which group of work-related requirements am I in` IS
    `s 57 WRA2007 11(3) the group the person falls into` (`s 57 WRA2007 11D(2) the person falls within section 11D` `I have limited capability for work and work-related activity` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `my responsibilities are regular and substantial caring responsibilities as regulations prescribe`) (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `the person I care for is severely disabled as regulations prescribe`) `s 39(1) the person is a member of a couple` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `I am responsible for the child, as the circumstances regulations specify`) `the age of the child in years` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `I am of a description prescribed for section 11D(2)(d)`)) (`s 57 WRA2007 11E(1) the person falls within section 11E` `s 39(1) the person is a member of a couple` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `I am responsible for the child, as the circumstances regulations specify`) `the age of the child in years` (`Under wra2, a number that may not be known` `the age that regulations prescribe` `I know the age that regulations prescribe`) (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `I am of a description prescribed for section 11E(1)(b)`))

@export Under section 57, may the Secretary of State require me to report this change in my circumstances (Welfare Reform Act 2007, section 11G(4))?
GIVEN `the change is relevant to the imposition of work-related requirements on me, or to my compliance with one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change relevant to the work-related requirements imposed on you, or to your compliance with one?
      `the change has been specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this kind of change been specified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 57, may the Secretary of State require me to report this change in my circumstances` IS
    `s 57 WRA2007 11G(4) the Secretary of State may require the person to report the change in circumstances` `the change is relevant to the imposition of work-related requirements on me, or to my compliance with one` `the change has been specified`

@export Under section 57, does a requirement imposed on me cease to have effect for 13 weeks (Welfare Reform Act 2007, section 11H(5))?
GIVEN `I have recently been a victim of domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you recently been a victim of domestic violence?
      `I am in the circumstances the regulations prescribe` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Are you in the circumstances the regulations prescribe for this protection?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 57, does a requirement imposed on me cease to have effect for 13 weeks` IS
    `s 57 WRA2007 11H(5) a requirement imposed on the person ceases to have effect for 13 weeks` `I have recently been a victim of domestic violence` (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `I am in the circumstances the regulations prescribe`)

@export Under section 57, is my failure sanctionable under section 11J (Welfare Reform Act 2007, section 11J(2))?
GIVEN `I failed to comply with a work-related requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with a work-related requirement?
      `I failed to comply with a requirement under section 11G` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with a requirement to attend an interview, provide information or report a change?
      `regulations treat my case as to a good reason` IS A `Under section 57, how regulations treat my reason` @desc How do the regulations treat your case as to whether you had a good reason?
      `on the facts I had a good reason` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc On the facts, taking into account the matters the regulations require or forbid, did you have a good reason?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 57, is my failure sanctionable under section 11J` IS
    `s 57 WRA2007 11J(2) the failure is sanctionable under section 11J` `I failed to comply with a work-related requirement` `I failed to comply with a requirement under section 11G` (`s 57(7)(b) WRA2007 Sch 2 para 10ZA the person has a good reason` (`Under section 57, regulations' treatment as a three-valued fact` `regulations treat my case as to a good reason`) (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `on the facts I had a good reason`))

@export Under section 57, is my award to be reduced under section 11J (Welfare Reform Act 2007, section 11J(1))?
GIVEN `I failed to comply with a work-related requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with a work-related requirement?
      `I failed to comply with a requirement under section 11G` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with a requirement to attend an interview, provide information or report a change?
      `regulations treat my case as to a good reason` IS A `Under section 57, how regulations treat my reason` @desc How do the regulations treat your case as to whether you had a good reason?
      `on the facts I had a good reason` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc On the facts, taking into account the matters the regulations require or forbid, did you have a good reason?
      `regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in my case` IS A `Under wra2, a yes, no or not-known answer` @desc Do regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 57, is my award to be reduced under section 11J` IS
    `s 57 WRA2007 11J(1) the award is to be reduced in accordance with section 11J` (`s 57 WRA2007 11J(2) the failure is sanctionable under section 11J` `I failed to comply with a work-related requirement` `I failed to comply with a requirement under section 11G` (`s 57(7)(b) WRA2007 Sch 2 para 10ZA the person has a good reason` (`Under section 57, regulations' treatment as a three-valued fact` `regulations treat my case as to a good reason`) (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `on the facts I had a good reason`))) (`Under wra2, the answer as a three-valued fact` `regulations provide that no reduction is to be made in my case`)

@export Under section 57, is the fixed period of my reduction within 26 weeks (Welfare Reform Act 2007, section 11J(4)(b))?
GIVEN `the first day of the reduction` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the reduction?
      `the last day of the reduction` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the reduction?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 57, is the fixed period of my reduction within 26 weeks` IS
