§ `Entitlement to work (sections 61 to 63)`

@export Under section 61, am I entitled to be in employment in the United Kingdom for the purposes of jobseeker's allowance (Jobseekers Act 1995, section 1(3A))?
GIVEN `I do not under the Immigration Act 1971 require leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you someone who does not need leave under the Immigration Act 1971 to enter or remain in the United Kingdom?
      `I have been granted such leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been granted leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom?
      `my leave is not invalid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your leave valid?
      `my leave has not for any reason ceased to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your leave still in effect (it has not ended for any reason)?
      `my leave is not subject to a condition preventing me from accepting any employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your leave free of any condition that prevents you from accepting employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 61, am I entitled to be in employment in the United Kingdom for the purposes of jobseeker's allowance` IS
    `s 61(3) JSA 1(3A) the person is entitled to be in employment in the United Kingdom` `I do not under the Immigration Act 1971 require leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom` `I have been granted such leave` `my leave is not invalid` `my leave has not for any reason ceased to have effect` `my leave is not subject to a condition preventing me from accepting any employment`

