GIVEN `I know whether I meet the residence and presence conditions the regulations set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `I meet the residence and presence conditions the regulations set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the conditions about residence and presence in Great Britain that the regulations set? (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
      `I am entitled to Scottish adult disability living allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to Scottish adult disability living allowance?
      `I am entitled to pension age disability payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to pension age disability payment?
      `I am entitled to adult disability payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to adult disability payment?
      `I am entitled to child disability payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to child disability payment?
      `my ability to carry out daily living activities is limited by my physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the assessment find that your ability to carry out daily living activities is limited by your physical or mental condition?
      `my ability to carry out daily living activities is severely limited by my physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the assessment find that your ability to carry out daily living activities is severely limited by your physical or mental condition?
      `I know whether I meet the required period condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `I meet the required period condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the "required period condition"? (The question under section 81 asks what it turns on.) (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
      `I suffer from a progressive disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suffer from a progressive disease?
      `the date I ask about` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you ask whether you are terminally ill? (day, month and year)
      `the date by which my death in consequence of the disease can reasonably be expected` IS A DATE @desc By what date can your death in consequence of the disease reasonably be expected? (If it is not expected in the foreseeable future, give a date far ahead, such as 1 January 2100.)
      `I have made a claim for personal independence payment expressly on the ground of terminal illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a claim for personal independence payment expressly on the ground that you are terminally ill?
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in completed years?
      `I have reached pensionable age within the meaning of the Pensions Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached pensionable age, as the rules in paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the Pensions Act 1995 work it out?
      `I know whether regulations give an exception to the bar at the relevant age that covers me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `regulations give an exception to the bar at the relevant age that covers me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations give an exception to the bar on entitlement after the relevant age that covers you? (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
      `a relevant EU Regulation applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Council Regulation (EC) No 1408/71 or Regulation (EC) No 883/2004 apply to you?
      `the United Kingdom is competent to pay me sickness benefits in cash for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period, is the United Kingdom the competent state for paying you sickness benefits in cash (for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Title III of the Regulation that applies)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 78(6), am I entitled to the daily living component at the standard rate` IS
    `s 78(6) the person is entitled to the daily living component, subject to the other provisions of Part 4 relating to entitlement`
        `my result at the standard rate, section 82 displacing section 78(1)`
        (LIST `s 77(3) the person is not barred for want of the prescribed residence and presence conditions` `I meet the residence and presence conditions the regulations set, as far as I know`,
              `s 77(4) the person is not barred by being entitled to a Scottish disability payment` `the Scottish disability payments I am entitled to`,
              `s 83(1) the person is not barred by having reached the relevant age` `me` `I have reached pensionable age within the meaning of the Pensions Act 1995` `regulations give an exception to the bar at the relevant age that covers me, as far as I know`,
              `s 84(1) the person is not barred from the daily living component by the United Kingdom not being the competent state` `a relevant EU Regulation applies to me` `the United Kingdom is competent to pay me sickness benefits in cash for the period`)
    WHERE
        `I meet the residence and presence conditions the regulations set, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a yes or no the person may be unable to give` `I know whether I meet the residence and presence conditions the regulations set` `I meet the residence and presence conditions the regulations set`
        `I meet the required period condition, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a yes or no the person may be unable to give` `I know whether I meet the required period condition` `I meet the required period condition`
        `regulations give an exception to the bar at the relevant age that covers me, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a yes or no the person may be unable to give` `I know whether regulations give an exception to the bar at the relevant age that covers me` `regulations give an exception to the bar at the relevant age that covers me`
        `the Scottish disability payments I am entitled to` MEANS
            concat (LIST (IF `I am entitled to Scottish adult disability living allowance` THEN LIST `s 95 Scottish adult disability living allowance` ELSE EMPTY),
                         (IF `I am entitled to pension age disability payment` THEN LIST `s 95 pension age disability payment` ELSE EMPTY),
                         (IF `I am entitled to adult disability payment` THEN LIST `s 95 adult disability payment` ELSE EMPTY),
                         (IF `I am entitled to child disability payment` THEN LIST `s 95 child disability payment` ELSE EMPTY))
        `I am terminally ill at the date I ask about` MEANS
            `s 82(4) the person is terminally ill at the time` `I suffer from a progressive disease` `the date I ask about` `the date by which my death in consequence of the disease can reasonably be expected`
        `section 82 applies to me` MEANS
            `s 82(1) this section applies to the person` `I am terminally ill at the date I ask about` `I have made a claim for personal independence payment expressly on the ground of terminal illness`
        `my result at the standard rate, section 82 displacing section 78(1)` MEANS
            `s 82(2) the result under section 78(1), section 82 displacing section 78(1)` `section 82 applies to me`
                (`s 78(1) the person is entitled to the daily living component at the standard rate` `my ability to carry out daily living activities is limited by my physical or mental condition` `I meet the required period condition, as far as I know`)
        `my result at the enhanced rate, section 82 displacing section 78(2)` MEANS
            `s 82(2) the person is entitled to the daily living component at the enhanced rate, section 82 displacing section 78(2)` `section 82 applies to me`
                (`s 78(2) the person is entitled to the daily living component at the enhanced rate` `my ability to carry out daily living activities is severely limited by my physical or mental condition` `I meet the required period condition, as far as I know`)
        `my own result under section 78(1) or (2), or section 82(2)` MEANS
            `s 78(6) the disjunction of the results` (LIST `my result at the standard rate, section 82 displacing section 78(1)`, `my result at the enhanced rate, section 82 displacing section 78(2)`)
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
                `reference` IS "claimant"                    -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads the reference
                `age in years` IS `my age in years`
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1900              -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads the date of birth
                `where the person is` IS `Greater London`     -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads where the person is
                `where the person lives` IS `Greater London`  -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads where the person lives

