        `my result at the enhanced rate, section 82 displacing section 78(2)` MEANS
            `s 82(2) the person is entitled to the daily living component at the enhanced rate, section 82 displacing section 78(2)` `section 82 applies to me`
                (`s 78(2) the person is entitled to the daily living component at the enhanced rate` `my ability to carry out daily living activities is severely limited by my physical or mental condition` `I meet the required period condition, as far as I know`)
        `my own result under section 78(1) or (2), or section 82(2)` MEANS
            `s 78(6) the disjunction of the results` (LIST `my result at the standard rate, section 82 displacing section 78(1)`, `my result at the enhanced rate, section 82 displacing section 78(2)`)
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
                `reference` IS "claimant"                    -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads the reference
                `age in years` IS `my age in years`
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1900              -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads the date of birth
                `where the person is` IS `Greater London`     -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads where the person is
                `where the person lives` IS `Greater London`  -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads where the person lives

§§ `Section 79 -- Mobility component`

@desc Only the section 79(1) conditions. It does not apply the other provisions of Part 4 that section 79(6) makes this subject to; the question under section 79(6) does.
@export Under section 79(1), do I satisfy the conditions for the mobility component at the standard rate?
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in completed years?
      `I know the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the standard rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the standard rate` IS A NUMBER @desc What age do the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the standard rate? (years) (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
      `my ability to carry out mobility activities is limited by my physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the assessment find that your ability to carry out mobility activities is limited by your physical or mental condition?
      `I know whether I meet the required period condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `I meet the required period condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the "required period condition"? (The question under section 81 asks what it turns on.) (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 79(1), do I satisfy the conditions for the mobility component at the standard rate` IS
    `s 79(1) the person is entitled to the mobility component at the standard rate` `my ability to carry out mobility activities is limited by my physical or mental condition` `I am of or over the age prescribed for section 79(1)` `I meet the required period condition, as far as I know`
    WHERE
        `the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the standard rate, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a number the person may be unable to give` `I know the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the standard rate` `the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the standard rate`
        `I meet the required period condition, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a yes or no the person may be unable to give` `I know whether I meet the required period condition` `I meet the required period condition`
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
                `reference` IS "claimant"                    -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads the reference
                `age in years` IS `my age in years`
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1900              -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads the date of birth
                `where the person is` IS `Greater London`     -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads where the person is
                `where the person lives` IS `Greater London`  -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads where the person lives
        `I am of or over the age prescribed for section 79(1)` MEANS
            `s 79(1)(a) the person is of or over the age prescribed` `me` `the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the standard rate, as far as I know`

@desc Only the section 79(2) conditions. It does not apply the other provisions of Part 4 that section 79(6) makes this subject to; the question under section 79(6) does.
@export Under section 79(2), do I satisfy the conditions for the mobility component at the enhanced rate?
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in completed years?
      `I know the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the enhanced rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the enhanced rate` IS A NUMBER @desc What age do the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the enhanced rate? (years) (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
      `my ability to carry out mobility activities is severely limited by my physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the assessment find that your ability to carry out mobility activities is severely limited by your physical or mental condition?
      `I know whether I meet the required period condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `I meet the required period condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the "required period condition"? (The question under section 81 asks what it turns on.) (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 79(2), do I satisfy the conditions for the mobility component at the enhanced rate` IS
    `s 79(2) the person is entitled to the mobility component at the enhanced rate` `my ability to carry out mobility activities is severely limited by my physical or mental condition` `I am of or over the age prescribed for section 79(2)` `I meet the required period condition, as far as I know`
    WHERE
        `the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the enhanced rate, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a number the person may be unable to give` `I know the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the enhanced rate` `the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the enhanced rate`
        `I meet the required period condition, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a yes or no the person may be unable to give` `I know whether I meet the required period condition` `I meet the required period condition`
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
                `reference` IS "claimant"                    -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads the reference
                `age in years` IS `my age in years`
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1900              -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads the date of birth
                `where the person is` IS `Greater London`     -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads where the person is
                `where the person lives` IS `Greater London`  -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads where the person lives
        `I am of or over the age prescribed for section 79(2)` MEANS
            `s 79(2)(a) the person is of or over the age prescribed` `me` `the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the enhanced rate, as far as I know`

@desc Only the section 79(7) bar, and only if regulations use the power. JUST FALSE means regulations bar you; NOTHING means whether they do has not been settled.
@export Under section 79(7), am I free of any bar from regulations about the unlikelihood of benefiting from enhanced mobility?
GIVEN `I know whether regulations bar my mobility component for the period because I am unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `regulations bar my mobility component for the period because I am unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations provide that you are not entitled to the mobility component for the period, because during all or most of it you are unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility? (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 79(7), am I free of any bar from regulations about the unlikelihood of benefiting from enhanced mobility` IS
    `s 79(7) the person is not barred by regulations about unlikelihood of benefiting from enhanced mobility` `regulations bar my mobility component for the period because I am unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility, as far as I know`
    WHERE
        `regulations bar my mobility component for the period because I am unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a yes or no the person may be unable to give` `I know whether regulations bar my mobility component for the period because I am unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility` `regulations bar my mobility component for the period because I am unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility`

-- Section 79(6): "This section is subject to the provisions of this Part, or regulations under it, relating to entitlement to the mobility component (see in particular sections 82 and 83)".
@desc The section 79(1) and (2) result at either rate, combined with the other Part 4 provisions on entitlement that this seat covers: sections 77(3), 77(4), 83(1) and 79(7). The required period condition is dropped for a person to whom section 82 applies (section 82(3)). It does not cover the bars on payment in sections 86 to 88 (those have their own questions) or any provision of regulations that is not among the sources. NOTHING means a regulation-dependent fact has not been settled; it is never a no.
@export Under section 79(6), am I entitled to the mobility component?
GIVEN `I know whether I meet the residence and presence conditions the regulations set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `I meet the residence and presence conditions the regulations set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the conditions about residence and presence in Great Britain that the regulations set? (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
      `I am entitled to Scottish adult disability living allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to Scottish adult disability living allowance?
      `I am entitled to pension age disability payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to pension age disability payment?
      `I am entitled to adult disability payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to adult disability payment?
      `I am entitled to child disability payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to child disability payment?
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in completed years?
      `I know the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the standard rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the standard rate` IS A NUMBER @desc What age do the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the standard rate? (years) (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
      `I know the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the enhanced rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the enhanced rate` IS A NUMBER @desc What age do the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the enhanced rate? (years) (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
      `my ability to carry out mobility activities is limited by my physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the assessment find that your ability to carry out mobility activities is limited by your physical or mental condition?
      `my ability to carry out mobility activities is severely limited by my physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the assessment find that your ability to carry out mobility activities is severely limited by your physical or mental condition?
      `I know whether I meet the required period condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `I meet the required period condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the "required period condition"? (The question under section 81 asks what it turns on.) (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
      `I suffer from a progressive disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suffer from a progressive disease?
      `the date I ask about` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you ask whether you are terminally ill? (day, month and year)
      `the date by which my death in consequence of the disease can reasonably be expected` IS A DATE @desc By what date can your death in consequence of the disease reasonably be expected? (If it is not expected in the foreseeable future, give a date far ahead, such as 1 January 2100.)
      `I have made a claim for personal independence payment expressly on the ground of terminal illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a claim for personal independence payment expressly on the ground that you are terminally ill?
      `I have reached pensionable age within the meaning of the Pensions Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached pensionable age, as the rules in paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the Pensions Act 1995 work it out?
      `I know whether regulations give an exception to the bar at the relevant age that covers me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `regulations give an exception to the bar at the relevant age that covers me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations give an exception to the bar on entitlement after the relevant age that covers you? (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
      `I know whether regulations bar my mobility component for the period because I am unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `regulations bar my mobility component for the period because I am unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations provide that you are not entitled to the mobility component for the period, because during all or most of it you are unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility? (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 79(6), am I entitled to the mobility component` IS
    `s 79(6) the person is entitled to the mobility component, subject to the other provisions of Part 4 relating to entitlement`
        `my own result under section 79(1) or (2)`
        (LIST `s 77(3) the person is not barred for want of the prescribed residence and presence conditions` `I meet the residence and presence conditions the regulations set, as far as I know`,
              `s 77(4) the person is not barred by being entitled to a Scottish disability payment` `the Scottish disability payments I am entitled to`,
              `s 83(1) the person is not barred by having reached the relevant age` `me` `I have reached pensionable age within the meaning of the Pensions Act 1995` `regulations give an exception to the bar at the relevant age that covers me, as far as I know`,
              `s 79(7) the person is not barred by regulations about unlikelihood of benefiting from enhanced mobility` `regulations bar my mobility component for the period because I am unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility, as far as I know`)
    WHERE
        `I meet the residence and presence conditions the regulations set, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a yes or no the person may be unable to give` `I know whether I meet the residence and presence conditions the regulations set` `I meet the residence and presence conditions the regulations set`
        `the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the standard rate, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a number the person may be unable to give` `I know the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the standard rate` `the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the standard rate`
        `the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the enhanced rate, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a number the person may be unable to give` `I know the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the enhanced rate` `the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the enhanced rate`
        `I meet the required period condition, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a yes or no the person may be unable to give` `I know whether I meet the required period condition` `I meet the required period condition`
        `regulations give an exception to the bar at the relevant age that covers me, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a yes or no the person may be unable to give` `I know whether regulations give an exception to the bar at the relevant age that covers me` `regulations give an exception to the bar at the relevant age that covers me`
        `regulations bar my mobility component for the period because I am unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a yes or no the person may be unable to give` `I know whether regulations bar my mobility component for the period because I am unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility` `regulations bar my mobility component for the period because I am unlikely to benefit from enhanced mobility`
        `the Scottish disability payments I am entitled to` MEANS
            concat (LIST (IF `I am entitled to Scottish adult disability living allowance` THEN LIST `s 95 Scottish adult disability living allowance` ELSE EMPTY),
                         (IF `I am entitled to pension age disability payment` THEN LIST `s 95 pension age disability payment` ELSE EMPTY),
                         (IF `I am entitled to adult disability payment` THEN LIST `s 95 adult disability payment` ELSE EMPTY),
                         (IF `I am entitled to child disability payment` THEN LIST `s 95 child disability payment` ELSE EMPTY))
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
                `reference` IS "claimant"                    -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads the reference
                `age in years` IS `my age in years`
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1900              -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads the date of birth
                `where the person is` IS `Greater London`     -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads where the person is
                `where the person lives` IS `Greater London`  -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads where the person lives
        `I am terminally ill at the date I ask about` MEANS
            `s 82(4) the person is terminally ill at the time` `I suffer from a progressive disease` `the date I ask about` `the date by which my death in consequence of the disease can reasonably be expected`
        `section 82 applies to me` MEANS
            `s 82(1) this section applies to the person` `I am terminally ill at the date I ask about` `I have made a claim for personal independence payment expressly on the ground of terminal illness`
        `the required period condition limb as it stands for me` MEANS
            `s 82(3) the required period condition limb of section 79(1)(c) and (2)(c), as it stands for the person` `section 82 applies to me` `I meet the required period condition, as far as I know`
        `my result at the standard rate` MEANS
            `s 79(1) the person is entitled to the mobility component at the standard rate` `my ability to carry out mobility activities is limited by my physical or mental condition`
                (`s 79(1)(a) the person is of or over the age prescribed` `me` `the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the standard rate, as far as I know`) `the required period condition limb as it stands for me`
        `my result at the enhanced rate` MEANS
            `s 79(2) the person is entitled to the mobility component at the enhanced rate` `my ability to carry out mobility activities is severely limited by my physical or mental condition`
                (`s 79(2)(a) the person is of or over the age prescribed` `me` `the age the regulations prescribe for the mobility component at the enhanced rate, as far as I know`) `the required period condition limb as it stands for me`
        `my own result under section 79(1) or (2)` MEANS
            `s 78(6) the disjunction of the results` (LIST `my result at the standard rate`, `my result at the enhanced rate`)

