    `sch 4 para 4 SPCA 3A(2) the second condition for housing credit is met` `the amount of the housing credit that would be payable if I were entitled to it` `the amount regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 3A(2), as far as I know`
    WHERE
        `the amount regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 3A(2), as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a number the person may be unable to give` `I know the amount regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 3A(2)` `the amount regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 3A(2)`

@desc Section 1(3)(c) of the State Pension Credit Act 2002 as amended, through the conditions in section 3A(1) and (2) (assumed, not ruled). NOTHING means a condition has not been settled.
@export Under schedule 4 paragraph 3, am I entitled to a housing credit?
GIVEN `I know whether I am liable to make payments in respect of the accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `I am liable to make payments in respect of the accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you liable to make payments in respect of the accommodation you occupy as your home? (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
      `I know whether I occupy the accommodation as my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `I occupy the accommodation as my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you occupy the accommodation as your home? (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
      `the amount of the housing credit that would be payable if I were entitled to it` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount of housing credit would be payable to you if you were entitled to it? (pounds)
      `I know the amount regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 3A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `the amount regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 3A(2)` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount do regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 3A(2) of the State Pension Credit Act 2002? (pounds) (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 4 paragraph 3, am I entitled to a housing credit` IS
    `sch 4 para 3 SPCA 1(3)(c) the claimant is entitled to a housing credit` `I satisfy the conditions in section 3A(1) and (2)`
    WHERE
        `I am liable to make payments in respect of the accommodation, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a yes or no the person may be unable to give` `I know whether I am liable to make payments in respect of the accommodation` `I am liable to make payments in respect of the accommodation`
        `I occupy the accommodation as my home, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a yes or no the person may be unable to give` `I know whether I occupy the accommodation as my home` `I occupy the accommodation as my home`
        `the amount regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 3A(2), as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a number the person may be unable to give` `I know the amount regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 3A(2)` `the amount regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 3A(2)`
        `the first condition for housing credit` MEANS
            `sch 4 para 4 SPCA 3A(1) the first condition for housing credit is met` `I am liable to make payments in respect of the accommodation, as far as I know` `I occupy the accommodation as my home, as far as I know`
        `the second condition for housing credit` MEANS
            `sch 4 para 4 SPCA 3A(2) the second condition for housing credit is met` `the amount of the housing credit that would be payable if I were entitled to it` `the amount regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 3A(2), as far as I know`
        `I satisfy the conditions in section 3A(1) and (2)` MEANS
            `sch 4 para 2 SPCA 1(2)(c)(iii) the claimant satisfies the conditions in section 3A(1) and (2)` `the first condition for housing credit` `the second condition for housing credit`

§ `Schedule 9 -- Personal independence payment: amendments`

@desc Section 64(1A), as inserted. NOTHING means the subsection lists allowances and does not say that no other allowance is within it.
