§ `Schedule 11 -- Power to require consideration of revision before appeal`

§§ `Paragraph 2 -- Vaccine Damage Payments Act 1979, section 4`

@desc Only the added power: it limits the right of appeal "only if" the earlier step was taken. JUST FALSE means the earlier step was not taken, so no right of appeal under regulations that so provide; NOTHING means the text does not say (regulations not settled, or the case is not one the added subsection covers). It does not give the right of appeal itself.
@export Under schedule 11 paragraph 2, is there a right of appeal against the decision on my vaccine damage payment claim (Vaccine Damage Payments Act 1979, section 4(1B))?
GIVEN `my address is in Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your address in Northern Ireland?
      `I know whether regulations require consideration before I can appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `regulations require consideration before I can appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations require that, in your case, there is a right of appeal only after the Secretary of State has considered whether to reverse the decision under section 3A? (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
      `the Secretary of State has considered whether to reverse the decision under section 3A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State considered whether to reverse the decision under section 3A?
      `the consideration satisfied the further conditions the regulations specify` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that consideration satisfy any further conditions the regulations specify (for example, that it was on an application)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 11 paragraph 2, is there a right of appeal against the decision on my vaccine damage payment claim (Vaccine Damage Payments Act 1979, section 4(1B))` IS
    `sch 11 para 2(2) VDPA 4(1B) there is a right of appeal against the decision` `my address is in Northern Ireland` `regulations require consideration before I can appeal, as far as I know` `the Secretary of State has considered whether to reverse the decision under section 3A` `the consideration satisfied the further conditions the regulations specify`
    WHERE
        `regulations require consideration before I can appeal, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a yes or no the person may be unable to give` `I know whether regulations require consideration before I can appeal` `regulations require consideration before I can appeal`

@desc Only the added power. JUST TRUE means regulations so provide and there is no right of appeal in accordance with the regulations requiring consideration first; NOTHING means the text does not say (it is a permission regulations may give).
@export Under schedule 11 paragraph 2, may my purported appeal be treated as an application to reverse the decision under section 3A?
GIVEN `I know whether regulations treat a purported appeal as an application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you answer the next question yet? Answer no if the regulations or a decision-maker have not settled it for you, or you do not know.
      `regulations treat a purported appeal as an application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations provide that a purported appeal may be treated as an application to reverse the decision under section 3A? (Ignored if you answered no to the question before this one.)
      `there is no right of appeal against my decision in accordance with the regulations requiring consideration first` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In accordance with those regulations, is there no right of appeal against your decision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 11 paragraph 2, may my purported appeal be treated as an application to reverse the decision under section 3A` IS
    `sch 11 para 2(3) VDPA 4(2)(c) a purported appeal may be treated as an application to reverse the decision under section 3A` `regulations treat a purported appeal as an application, as far as I know` `there is no right of appeal against my decision in accordance with the regulations requiring consideration first`
    WHERE
        `regulations treat a purported appeal as an application, as far as I know` MEANS
            `wra3 seat a yes or no the person may be unable to give` `I know whether regulations treat a purported appeal as an application` `regulations treat a purported appeal as an application`

